---
import Card from '../../components/ui/Card.astro';
import Table from '../../components/ui/Table.astro';
import Specimen from '../Specimen.astro';
---
<Specimen title="Basic" code={'<Card>\n    <Table label="Settings">\n        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Value</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>…</tbody>\n    </Table>\n</Card>'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes">
        <p>The Stride table: no rules between rows, a recessed header row in small muted capitals, and roomy cells. It has no surface of its own, so it is normally set in an unpadded card.</p>
        <p>The wrapper scrolls sideways when the table is wider than its container. It is a labelled region that takes focus, so keyboard users can scroll it; <code>label</code> names it. Mark header cells with <code>scope</code>.</p>
    </Fragment>
    <Card>
        <Table label="Settings">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Value</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td>Region</td><td>EU</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Plan</td><td>Pro</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </Table>
    </Card>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Striped" code={'<Table label="People" striped>…</Table>'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>Alternate rows take the alternate surface. Row header cells (<code>&lt;th scope="row"&gt;</code>) are set in the heading colour.</p></Fragment>
    <Card>
        <Table label="People, striped" striped>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Channel</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><th scope="row">Ada</th><td>Chat</td><td><span class="badge badge-success">Online</span></td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Grace</th><td>Mail</td><td><span class="badge">Offline</span></td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Alan</th><td>Call</td><td><span class="badge badge-warning">Away</span></td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Katherine</th><td>Chat</td><td><span class="badge badge-success">Online</span></td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </Table>
    </Card>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Hover" code={'<Table label="People" hover>…</Table>'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>Rows highlight under the pointer. Use it for tables whose rows link somewhere; combined with striping, a hovered stripe goes one step deeper.</p></Fragment>
    <div class="grid grid-2">
        <Card>
            <Table label="People, hover" hover>
                <thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Channel</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Ada</th><td>Chat</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Grace</th><td>Mail</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Alan</th><td>Call</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </Table>
        </Card>
        <Card>
            <Table label="People, striped with hover" striped hover>
                <thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Channel</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Ada</th><td>Chat</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Grace</th><td>Mail</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Alan</th><td>Call</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </Table>
        </Card>
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Wide tables and captions" code={'<Table label="Releases">\n    <caption>Releases by quarter</caption>\n    …\n</Table>'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>A wide table scrolls inside its card instead of stretching the page; tab to it and use the arrow keys. A <code>&lt;caption&gt;</code> renders as a muted line above the header row.</p></Fragment>
    <Card>
        <Table label="Releases by quarter">
            <caption>Releases by quarter</caption>
            <thead>
                <tr><th scope="col">Package</th><th scope="col">Q1</th><th scope="col">Q2</th><th scope="col">Q3</th><th scope="col">Q4</th><th scope="col">Total</th><th scope="col">Notes</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><th scope="row">Package one</th><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>1</td><td>4</td><td>10</td><td>A longer note that keeps the table wide on small screens.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Package two</th><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>5</td><td>Another long note so the columns need room.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Package three</th><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3</td><td>A third note.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </Table>
    </Card>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="On a dark band" surface="dark">
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>The striped table in the dark palette.</p></Fragment>
    <Card>
        <Table label="People on dark" striped hover>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Channel</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><th scope="row">Ada</th><td>Chat</td><td><span class="badge badge-success">Online</span></td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Grace</th><td>Mail</td><td><span class="badge">Offline</span></td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Alan</th><td>Call</td><td><span class="badge badge-warning">Away</span></td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </Table>
    </Card>
</Specimen>
